{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban the practice of\u2019 free pitching\u2019 by agencies and freelancers to brands",
        "additional_details": "Brands ask agencies to pitch work for free as standard in the UK Creative Industry. The process is extractive, impacting independent business the hardest. Brands with multi-million dollar budgets should not be allowed to ask agencies to embark on work for their business as part of a pitch without paying them for that service. Business intelligence and creative IP is being extracted by brands in some instances - and work that has been created \u201cfor free\u201d is being used without engaging the agencies the ideas were stolen from.",
        "background": "Ban 'free pitching' in law so that brands must remunerate agencies and freelancers for pitches or use other ways of selecting whom to work with - e.g. brands could look at past work, pricing and reputation as grounds to engage them, as you would in other professions (e.g. trade).",
